# `-d share` only — the SHARE-backed LIBRARY on the Unraid box.
# Read as [.kamal/secrets-common, .kamal/secrets.share].
#
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY OF SECRETS. A share container holds NO storage credential: its library is a
# mounted directory at LIBRARY_PATH, so there is nothing to sign for. config/deploy.share.yml
# re-declares env.secret as [RAILS_MASTER_KEY] precisely to DROP the chunk secret it would
# otherwise inherit, and RAILS_MASTER_KEY plus the registry password both come from
# .kamal/secrets-common.
#
# This file exists to say that on purpose. Kamal skips a missing destination file without
# complaint (secrets_files does `select { File.exist? }`), so "no file" and "no secrets needed"
# look identical from the outside — and the next person to add a share credential would otherwise
# have to rediscover which file it goes in. Add it HERE, not in secrets-common: everything in
# secrets-common is parsed and executed by every other destination too.
